  "label": "Stereotype: Young men as untrustworthy or unreliable",
  "description": "The meme's sarcastic tone and the phrase 'then i don't wanna see what they call shame' imply that the group's 'pride' is so extreme or inappropriate that it makes 'shame' seem even more undesirable. This relies on the stereotype that young men (or certain groups) are inherently untrustworthy or unreliable, making their 'pride' seem even more dangerous or offensive. This stereotype is often used to justify negative judgments or dismissive attitudes toward certain groups.",
